 "kind": "knowledge",
 "definition": "In Marxian economics, the ratio of the capital spent on machinery and materials to the capital spent on wages.",
 "description": {
  "text": "A concept from Karl Marx's theory of capital, derived from the value composition and technical composition of capital. The technical composition measures the relation between constant capital (plant, equipment, materials) and variable capital (wage workers).",
